    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65937" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλδω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>soften by boiling</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέντα βοὸς μέλδοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					309
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυθομένοις μέλδουσιν ἅμ᾽ ἰχθύσιν
					οὐλοὸν ἅλμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					6.464
				</span></i>
			:—<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in 
				Med.
			 (or 
				Pass.
			), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς δὲ λέβης ζεῖ ἔνδον . . , κνίσην
					μελδόμενος ἁπαλοτρεφέος σιάλοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.363
				</span></i>
			 (vv. ll. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνίσῃ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελδομένου</span>):—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάρκες μελδόμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					108
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. Skt. <i>mṛdús</i>, Lat.
				<i>mollis</i> 'soft', O<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>
			<i>meltan</i> 'melt', ON orse <i>maltr</i> 'rotten', Gr.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βλαδύς</span>.)</div>
